  "_": [
    "OpenSSL 3 root-to-signing-key-to-revocation-to-head-to-manifest fixture for issues #660 and #693.",
    "Private keys are discarded. Godot consumes only signed objects and public root keys.",
    "Certificate, revocation and revocation-head signatures cover RFC 8785 JCS with root_signature excluded.",
    "Manifest signatures cover RFC 8785 JCS with signature excluded.",
    "Every revocation_head_* OBJECT is genuinely root-signed, so each is refused for its stated reason and not for a broken signature.",
    "revocation_head_forged_root_signature is the deliberate exception: it signs a LOWERED floor with the wrong root, so every other check passes and only root authentication can refuse it.",
    "cross_channel_manifest + beta_revocation_head are BOTH genuine: a live-labelled manifest embedding the beta channel real root-signed revocation stream, paired with the beta real current head. They agree with each other, so only binding to installed.revocation_head_url refuses them."
